      <title>The 2-Ingredient French Technique I Use to Make the Best Chicken Wing Sauce</title>
      <link>https://www.thekitchn.com/hot-sauce-beurre-monte-23768700?utm_source=RSS&amp;utm_medium=feed&amp;utm_campaign=Category%2FChannel%3A+main</link>
      <description>For years, I made my chicken wing sauce by pouring melted butter into hot sauce and stirring. It was simple, and it worked. But then I made a tiny tweak — like, really tiny — and I’ve never looked back. Now I make a hot sauce beurre monté, which gives you a smoother, thicker sauce that clings to wings instead of sliding off. It’s a simple technique, but it completely changes the texture. The sauce stays glossy, balanced, and slightly creamy without tasting heavy. READ MORE...</description>
